# Store and check out every file byte-exact: no line-ending conversion.
# Hundreds of tracked receipts pin other tracked files by SHA-256 of their on-disk
# bytes, and those files mix LF and CRLF. Normalization (text=auto with
# core.autocrlf) would change the bytes on checkout and break every such pin.
* -text

# MMR-259: the magic-ground decal texture sources and the module's published packs (with the editor's working packages) are
# release inputs: binary, large, kept in Git LFS. (Pointer files are LF text written by git-lfs; the receipts above do not pin them.)
Modules/MNBL.ProceduralWorld/AssetSources/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Modules/MNBL.ProceduralWorld/AssetPackages/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Modules/MNBL.ProceduralWorld/Assets/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# MMR-261 (RT-37): every producer build a campaign may cast with, by SHA-256 (worldgen/producer-archive.json). Release inputs: kept, never rebuilt.
Modules/MNBL.ProceduralWorld/Producers/** filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
